               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 77-year-old male, who presented on 29/09/1982 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. Diagnostic workup including blood tests, abdominal ultrasound, and physical examination confirmed the diagnosis. Given his age and clinical presentation, prompt surgical intervention was deemed necessary. The patient underwent a laparoscopic appendectomy on 30/09/1982 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, he received intravenous fluids, analgesics, and prophylactic antibiotics. Wound care was provided, and recovery was uneventful. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. The patient was mobilised early with physiotherapy support and discharged home on 02/10/1982 in good general condition. Please ensure appropriate follow-up and wound review in the coming days.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
